Each Box object stores a specific type of data, but the code for the Box class remains the same. This improves reusability and simplifies maintenance, as you can work with any type of data without duplicating class logic.

Generics can also be used for utilities. Let's see an example:

```kotlin
// Generic function to process lists
fun <T> List<T>.processEach(action: (T) -> Unit) {
    forEach { item -> action(item) }
}
// Use with different types:
val numbers = listOf(33, 3, 38)
numbers.processEach { println("Number: $it") }
val names = listOf("Noemi", "Viena", "Jose")
